			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add stub utilities for PerformanceDashboard metrics\n\nIntroduce `DashboardHelpers` module under `Source/IPC/Enhanced/PerformanceDashboard` to provide deterministic, side-effect-free utility functions for the performance monitoring system.\n\nThe implementation includes stub functions for retrieving process memory and CPU usage (returning fixed values until platform metrics are wired) and UUID generators for trace, span, and alert identifiers. Additionally, a `metric_type_name` helper maps `MetricType` variants to human-readable display strings for the dashboard UI.\n\nThis change exports the new module in `mod.rs`, establishing the foundational layer for the PerformanceDashboard IPC feature while adhering to the pure function architecture for testability.",
			"SHA": "e4c272b226471882b469bd9020eb70cb523cf39c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:07:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1568,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Clarify logger command fallback handling\n\nUpdate the comment block for logger commands (`logger:log`, `logger:warn`, etc.) in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`. The inline acknowledgment explicitly states that these high-frequency calls are now primarily managed by the `IS_HIGH_FREQUENCY` fast-path short-circuit established in recent commits.\n\nThe fallback arms in the `mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatcher are described as a safety net to ensure `Mountain.dev_log` receives output if the high-frequency detection logic changes or fails. This aligns the documentation with the current architectural optimization for the IPC dispatch layer.",
			"SHA": "db5faf8431473f060005b186245adfebef81bd7d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
